#
# This is EXACTLY the data used by main.nr's own `count_1_satisfies_circuit` test -- the
# ONE positive nargo test that exercises the FULL main() (header-chain continuity + condition
# (e)'s real ed25519 boundary-signature binding via `test_boundary_fixture()` +
# `call_main_with_test_boundary`); currently passing (`nargo test`, 10/10 pass, this session).
#
# rt_new is hash_header({prev_hash:111, fsm_state:2, withdrawal_locked:1, state_root:1000}) via
# the raw Poseidon2 t=4 permutation (std::hash::poseidon2_permutation) -- cross-verified
# byte-for-byte against x/sovereignty/types.HashHeader's Go port on this exact toolchain
# (gnark-crypto v0.21.0 vs. nargo 1.0.0-beta.22; see circuit/README.md's "Poseidon2
# Verification History").
#
# first_height/validators/first_block/last_block below are test_boundary_fixture()'s own
# hardcoded, ground-truthed 7-validator set (5-of-7 real ed25519 signatures, >2/3 quorum
# by power). first_block and last_block reuse the SAME witness, matching
# call_main_with_test_boundary -- these 5 real signatures were captured signing one shared
# message, valid for this fixture only; real production data has a genuinely different
# first/last block and a genuinely different timestamp per validator (BoundaryBlockWitness's
# own doc comment in main.nr explains why timestamp_content is per-validator, not shared).
#
# validator_set_hash below is validator_set_hash_bytes reduced mod the BN254 Fr modulus, not
# the raw big-endian byte concatenation -- main.nr's reduce_to_field does this reduction
# in-circuit automatically, so a Prover.toml value that skips it (the naive concatenation
# exceeds the modulus for this fixture's bytes) fails `nargo execute` with "exceeds field
# modulus" before any circuit logic even runs. first_block_hash/last_block_hash didn't need
# reduction here only because this fixture's block_hash_bytes ([1,2,...,32]) happens to stay
# under the modulus -- don't assume that holds for arbitrary bytes.
#
# Field ordering matters in this file: TOML requires every top-level scalar/array key
# (rt_last..validator_set_hash_bytes) before any [table]/[[array-of-tables]] section, and
# [[headers]] must come LAST (after [validators]/[first_block]/[last_block]) -- matches the
# order `nargo execute`'s own real Prover.toml (this crate's benchmark harness output) uses.
#
# Slots 2..256 are padding (unconstrained once count=1 -- see main.nr's `active` gate):
# their values are irrelevant, zero-filled here for clarity.
#
# To use: cp Prover.toml.example Prover.toml, then `nargo execute witness`.

